ELIXPO LICENSE
==============

This repository is part of the Elixpo ecosystem and is licensed under the
Elixpo licensing standard, the same standard that applies to every Elixpo
repository. Product-specific terms for this repository are declared in the
NOTICE file at the repository root (the "notice board"), which must be read
together with this LICENSE.

The LICENSES/ directory holds the canonical texts; this file is the pointer.

This repository is Orchard, the package registry of Plumlang. It holds
three kinds of things, under three grants, and the packages people publish,
which keep their own licences.

CODE
====

All code in this repository (tools/, the workflows and actions under
.github/, and any scripts and configuration) is provided under:

	SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT WITH Plumlang-trademarks

Being under the terms of the MIT License, as set out in:

	LICENSES/preferred/MIT

CONTENT
=======

The documentation and other written content (README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,
the issue forms' text) is provided under:

	SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0 WITH Plumlang-trademarks

Being under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License, as set out in:

	LICENSES/preferred/CC-BY-4.0

INDEX METADATA
==============

The index itself, everything under index/ and the file search.json (package
names, versions, checksums, dependencies, descriptions, keywords, owners and
dates), is dedicated to the public domain under:

	SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0

As set out in:

	LICENSES/preferred/CC0-1.0

so that anyone may mirror, search and build on the index without
conditions. Descriptions and keywords are submitted by package authors, who
agree to this dedication by publishing.

PACKAGES
========

The bundles under packages/ are the published packages. Each keeps the
licence its authors chose, named in its plum.toml (`license`) and its
LICENSE file; this repository grants nothing over them. The example package
under examples/hello-orchard/ is under the MIT License, as its LICENSE says.

EXCEPTION (names, marks, and royalties)
=======================================

The code and content grants above carry an explicit trademark and naming
exception:

	LICENSES/exceptions/Plumlang-trademarks

which also incorporates the Elixpo reservations in:

	LICENSES/exceptions/Oreo-trademarks

The licences grant rights to the files as files. They do NOT grant rights
to the Plumlang, Orchard, Elixpo or Oreo names or brands, nor the right to
offer a competing registry or service under them.

NOTICE BOARD (per-product reservations)
=======================================

Reservations for this repository, such as the Orchard name and the official
index, are declared in:

	NOTICE

THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
===================

Third-party components keep their own licences:

	LICENSES/notices/notice-board
	LICENSES/README.md

CONTRIBUTIONS
=============

By submitting a contribution to this repository you agree that it is licensed
inbound under this standard (MIT for code, CC-BY-4.0 for content, CC0-1.0 for
index metadata) and that you have the right to submit it. A package you
publish stays under its own licence. The Developer Certificate of Origin
(https://developercertificate.org) applies to every commit. We do not require
a CLA.

